@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Liberty HomeCare home insurance rules, document code UW-RPP-W-001-06-V.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/liberty-homecare.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of
-- liberty-homecare.pdf (sha256 f8c92ddb...5da27969), fetched from libertyinsurance.com.vn
-- and read as published on 2026-10-06. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that text and is
-- generated by tools/vnsrc.py; no Vietnamese here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. Dates are calendar dates (IMPORT daydate).
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence (the Insured, a loss
-- adjuster, a neighbour, the Policy Summary itself) could testify to the fact. Whether the
-- fact makes the Insurer liable is a rule, and lives in the module for the clause that says so.
--
-- TWO INPUT CONVENTIONS THAT EVERY CALLER MUST KNOW (NOTES.md section 1):
-- * A field typed `LIST OF A description of property` or `LIST OF A circumstance of a loss`
--   is a set of ticked boxes. It lists every description or circumstance in the enumeration
--   that is established for this case; one that is not listed is established NOT to apply.
--   These are the facts the cover clauses, exclusions and carve-backs turn on, one constructor
--   per phrase of the source, so that a case reads as the adjuster's findings.
-- * Everything the document leaves to the Policy Summary (Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm) is a field of
--   `The Policy Summary` with no default. Where the Summary may state nothing, the field is a
--   MAYBE and NOTHING means "the Summary states none"; a rule that needs the figure refuses.

§ `Nouns for Liberty HomeCare (UW-RPP-W-001-06-V)`

§§ `The parties and what they do`

-- Who owes or holds what. The Insurer is defined; the Insured is the person named in the
-- Policy Summary; the domestic helper appears in Part 3.
-- src:55 | Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:56 | Là (những) người được xác định là người được bảo hiểm trong Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm.
-- src:57 | Công Ty Bảo Hiểm
-- src:58 | Là Công ty TNHH Bảo hiểm Liberty.
DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured`
    `the Insurer`
    `the domestic helper`

-- The acts the document makes the subject of a duty, a power or a prohibition. Each is
-- something a witness could say happened, and when. Clause references are to NOTES.md section 2.
DECLARE `An act under the policy` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice of the event with full particulars`              -- GC4(a); Part 2 condition 1
    `forward every writ, summons, court order or notice on receipt`       -- GC4(b); Part 2 condition 1
    `admit, negotiate, offer, promise or pay without written consent`     -- GC4(c); Part 2 condition 2
    `notify the police`                                                   -- GC4(d)
    `act to minimise the loss`                                            -- GC4(e)
    `disclose all other insurances`                                       -- GC4(f)
    `deliver a written claim with particulars and evidence`               -- GC4(g)
    `pay the claim`                                                       -- Part 1 scope; Part 2
    `keep purchase receipts or proof of value`                            -- Part 1, proof of value
    `take reasonable precautions`                                         -- GC12
    `enter and take possession of the premises or property`              -- GC5(a)-(d)
    `obstruct the Insurer in exercising its powers`                       -- GC5
    `abandon property to the Insurer`                                     -- GC5
    `supply plans, specifications, quantities and particulars`            -- GC6
    `do what is required to enforce subrogation`                          -- GC8
    `submit the dispute to VIAC`                                          -- GC10
    `send written notice of cancellation by registered post`              -- GC11, the Insurer
    `send written notice of cancellation`                                 -- GC11, the Insured
    `refund premium`                                                      -- GC11
    `take over the defence or settlement of the claim`                    -- Part 2 condition 2
    `pay the limit or a lesser sum in settlement`                         -- Part 2 condition 3
    `observe the terms of the policy as if the Insured`                   -- Part 3, domestic helper

§§ `The Policy Summary`

-- The document leaves to the Policy Summary the Insured, the Period of Insurance, the items
-- insured, the sums insured, the Limits of Liability and "other conditions":
-- src:62 | Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm
-- src:63 | Là văn bản cấu thành một bộ phận không thể tách rời của Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm, trong đó cung cấp chi
-- src:64 | tiết về (những) Người Được Bảo Hiểm, Thời Hạn Bảo Hiểm, các hạng mục được bảo hiểm, số tiền bảo
-- src:65 | hiểm của (những) Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm, Giới Hạn Trách Nhiệm và các điều kiện khác được áp dụng.
-- So each of these is an input. A sum insured is NOTHING where the item is not insured under
-- Part 1; a limit or a Deductible is NOTHING where the Summary states none.
-- `the annual premium` is the "Phí Bảo hiểm năm" of the GC11 short-period scale.
-- The deductible is recorded per Part because GC13 speaks of the highest Deductible where one
-- loss gives rise to claims under several Parts:
-- src:977 | Nếu có bất kỳ tổn thất hoặc thiệt hại nào dẫn đến yêu cầu bồi thường cho nhiều Phần của Hợp
-- src:978 | Đồng Bảo Hiểm, chỉ có một Mức Miễn Thường cao nhất được áp dụng.
DECLARE `The Policy Summary` HAS
    `the Period of Insurance begins`                          IS A DATE
    `the Period of Insurance ends`                            IS A DATE
    `the sum insured on the Home`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the sum insured on the Contents`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 1 Limit of Liability`                           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period`            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 2 limit for food and drink`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 1 Deductible`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 2 Deductible`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Part 3 Deductible`                                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the Insured is named under Part 3`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the domestic helper benefit is named`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the construction of the Home is specially provided for`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the annual premium`                                      IS A NUMBER

§§ `The Insured and the premises`

DECLARE `The Insured person` HAS
    `date of birth`                                            IS A DATE
    `owns the Home or is legally responsible for its care`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a tenant of the Home`                                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- What kind of building the Home is. The first two are the kinds the definition of the Home
-- names; the rest are the kinds exclusion (c) names. NOTES.md fork F3 and finding 1.
-- src:74 | Là căn nhà hoặc căn hộ chung cư để ở tại Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm được nêu trong Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng
-- src:93 | (c) khách sạn, nhà nghỉ, bệnh xá, nhà trọ, các loại nhà và căn hộ, căn hộ có chủ quyền theo tầng hoặc
-- src:94 | nhà lưu động (được cố định hoặc không cố định tại đất của ngôi nhà);
DECLARE `A kind of building` IS ONE OF
    `a house`                                   -- căn nhà
    `an apartment in an apartment building`     -- căn hộ chung cư
    `a hotel`
    `a motel or guest house`
    `an infirmary`
    `a boarding house`
    `a strata-title apartment`
    `a mobile home`
    `another kind of building`

-- The facts the definitions of the Insured Location and the Home turn on.
-- `walls of concrete, brick or stone` and `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible
-- metal sheet`: the construction sentence of the Home definition.
-- src:78 | Ngôi Nhà được xây bằng bê tông, gạch hoặc đá và được lợp mái bê tông, ngói, đá phiến, các tấm hoặc
-- src:79 | bản kim loại được chế tạo hoàn toàn từ các chất khoáng không cháy, trừ khi có quy định đặc biệt trong
-- src:80 | Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm.
-- `part used as an office`, `office use approved`: the parentheses in both definitions.
-- `enclosed by walls or fences`: Insured Peril 9 (theft) requires it.
-- `some part is lent, let or sublet`: Insured Peril 9 exclusion (c).
-- `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods`: General Exclusion 8.
DECLARE `The insured premises` HAS
    `the kind of building`                                     IS A `A kind of building`
    `at the address in the Policy Summary`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured's principal personal residence`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `used wholly or mainly as the Insured's private residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part used as an office`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `office use approved by the authorities`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `used for a trade or business other than an office`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `walls of concrete, brick or stone`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible metal sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under construction`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `being demolished or vacant pending demolition`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a temporary building or structure`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `enclosed by walls or fences`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `some part is lent, let or sublet`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The contract-level facts: who the policy is issued to, and whether cover attached.
-- `issued to a company`, `the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`: Part 3 death benefit.
-- The three attachment facts are the Introduction's:
-- src:21 | Trừ khi Công Ty Bảo Hiểm đã đồng ý ban hành Giấy Chứng Nhận Bảo Hiểm và/hoặc Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp
-- src:22 | Đồng Bảo Hiểm, trách nhiệm bảo hiểm của Công Ty Bảo Hiểm chỉ bắt đầu có hiệu lực khi Công Ty Bảo
-- src:23 | Hiểm nhận được và chấp nhận Giấy Yêu Cầu Bảo Hiểm đã điền đầy đủ và Phí Bảo Hiểm đã được
-- src:24 | thanh toán đầy đủ trong thời hạn quy định.
DECLARE `The policy` HAS
    `the Policy Summary`                                       IS A `The Policy Summary`
    `the Insured`                                              IS A `The Insured person`
    `the premises`                                             IS A `The insured premises`
    `issued to a company`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insurer agreed to issue a Certificate or the Policy Summary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insurer received and accepted a completed Proposal Form`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premium was paid in full within the prescribed time`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premium paid`                                         IS A NUMBER

§§ `Property, and where it was`

-- The three things Part 1 insures, each with its own sum insured.
-- src:294 | Trường hợp xảy ra tổn thất, phá hủy hoặc thiệt hại về vật chất bất ngờ không lường trước được đối với
-- src:295 | Ngôi Nhà, Chi Phí Tân Trang/Cải Tạo và Tài Sản Bên Trong Nhà phát sinh trong Thời Hạn Bảo Hiểm
DECLARE `A Part 1 item` IS ONE OF
    `the Home`
    `the Renovation Costs`
    `the Contents`

-- Whose property it is. Contents must belong to the Insured or the Insured's Family, or be
-- property for whose loss either is legally responsible:
-- src:112 | Là các mục dưới đây, khi chúng tồn tại trong Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm, và thuộc về Người Được Bảo Hiểm,
-- src:113 | Gia Đình Người Được Bảo Hiểm hoặc sự tổn thất, thiệt hại của các tài sản này sẽ do Người Được Bảo
-- src:114 | Hiểm hoặc Gia Đình Người Được Bảo Hiểm chịu trách nhiệm về mặt pháp lý.
-- A relative is described by the facts the definition of the Family (Gia Đình Người Được Bảo
-- Hiểm) turns on: the relation, and whether the relative regularly lives with the Insured at
-- the Insured Location. Whether that makes the relative Family is a rule (fork F5):
-- src:160 | Gia Đình Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:161 | Là vợ/chồng, con cái và những thân nhân của Người Được Bảo Hiểm thường xuyên sống với Người
-- src:162 | Được Bảo Hiểm tại Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm.
DECLARE `A relation` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse`
    `a child`
    `another relative`

DECLARE `An owner of property` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured`
    `a relative of the Insured`
        HAS `relation`                                         IS A `A relation`
            `regularly lives with the Insured at the Insured Location` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another person, for whose loss the Insured or Family is legally responsible`
    `a domestic helper`
    `another person`

-- Where the property was when the loss happened. "In the open" (“Ngoài trời”) is defined by
-- Insured Peril 5 in terms of these places:
-- src:237 | “Ngoài trời” giới hạn ở Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm và bao gồm các kiến trúc và những phần không thể
-- src:238 | khóa lại của Ngôi Nhà. “Ngoài trời” còn có nghĩa là ở trong hoặc trên một loại xe hơi, xe gắn máy,
-- src:239 | toa moóc hoặc nhà lưu động, tại Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm, dù những xe này có khóa hay không.
DECLARE `A place where property was` IS ONE OF
    `inside a lockable part of the Home`
    `in a structure or part of the Home that cannot be locked`
    `outdoors at the Insured Location`
    `in or on a vehicle, trailer or caravan at the Insured Location`
    `away from the Insured Location`
    `in transit`

-- What the property is. A tick-box list (see the header): an item may fit several
-- descriptions, and the definitions are read off them. One constructor per phrase of the
-- source; the clause each belongs to is beside it.
DECLARE `A description of property` IS ONE OF
    -- The Home (Ngôi Nhà), the building itself and limbs (a)-(d) of "includes":
    `the house or apartment itself`
    `an outbuilding, garage, fixture or improvement`                       -- Home incl. (a)
    `an in-ground pool, tennis court, in-ground spa, sauna, jetty or pontoon` -- Home incl. (a)
    `used for domestic purposes`                                           -- Home incl. (a), qualifier
    `fixed lighting, wall, ceiling or fixed floor covering`                -- Home incl. (b)
    `a service above or below ground`                                      -- Home incl. (c)
    `owned by the Insured or the Insured must repair, replace or pay for it` -- Home incl. (c), qualifier
    `landscaping`                                                          -- Home incl. (d)
    `a paved path or paved driveway`                                       -- Home incl. (d)
    `a retaining wall or garden wall`                                      -- Home incl. (d); Peril 5 excl. (c)
    `a fence or gate`                                                      -- Home incl. (d); Peril 5 excl. (c)
    `on the land of the Home`                                              -- Home incl. (d), qualifier
    -- The Home, "does not include":
    `a carpet, curtain or internal blind`                                  -- Home excl. (a)
    `an unpaved path or driveway of earth or gravel`                       -- Home excl. (b)
    `trees, shrubs, grass or other living plants`                          -- Home excl. (h); Contents excl. (b); Peril 5 excl. (e)
    `soil, sand, gravel, bark or mulch`                                    -- Home excl. (h); Contents excl. (b)
    `a pot plant`                                                          -- Contents excl. (b), carve-back
    -- Renovation Costs (Chi Phí Tân Trang/Cải Tạo):
    `an improvement, fitting or decoration made by the Insured as tenant`
    `a built-in cabinet, cupboard or air-conditioning system installed by the Insured`
    -- Contents (Tài Sản Bên Trong Nhà), "includes":
    `furniture, a refrigerator, washing machine or similar household good` -- Contents incl. (a)
    `audio-visual equipment`                                               -- Contents incl. (a)
    `photographic, video or sports equipment`                              -- Contents incl. (a); excl. (j), F-contents-j
    `a musical instrument`                                                 -- Contents incl. (a)
    `a carpet, laid or not`                                                -- Contents incl. (a)
    `personal effects, normally carried or worn on the person`             -- Contents incl. (a)
    `a TV or radio antenna, antenna fitting or mast, or a satellite dish`  -- Contents incl. (b)
    `a golf buggy, garden appliance or motorised wheelchair`               -- Contents incl. (c)
    `required to be registered`                                            -- Contents incl. (c), qualifier
    `office furniture or equipment used for the Insured's own business in the Home` -- Contents incl. (d)
    `tools or equipment used to earn income`                               -- Contents incl. (e)
    -- Contents, "does not include":
    `a fish, bird or other animal`                                         -- Contents excl. (a)
    `a motor vehicle licensed for road use, a caravan or a trailer`        -- Contents excl. (c)
    `a watercraft`                                                         -- Contents excl. (d)
    `an aircraft or aircraft accessory`                                    -- Contents excl. (e)
    `an aircraft that cannot be piloted`                                   -- Contents excl. (e), carve-back
    `a part, key, lock or alarm of a vehicle, caravan, trailer, aircraft or watercraft` -- Contents excl. (f)
    `held unlawfully by the Insured`                                       -- Contents excl. (g)
    `kept unsafely and unlawfully`                                         -- Contents excl. (g)
    `equipment for developing or producing an illegal substance`           -- Contents excl. (g)
    `cash or coins`                                                        -- Contents excl. (h); Part 3 helper
    `a negotiable instrument`                                              -- Contents excl. (h)
    `jewellery, gold, silver or other precious metal, or a precious stone` -- Contents excl. (i)
    `a work of art, picture or other artwork`                              -- Contents excl. (i)
    `furs, fine glassware or crystal`                                      -- Contents excl. (i)
    `an antique or an item of special value`                               -- Contents excl. (i)
    `a laptop computer, mobile phone or camera`                            -- Contents excl. (j)
    `an item normally carried away from the Insured Location`              -- Contents excl. (j)
    `business or retail stock`                                             -- Contents excl. (k)
    -- Elsewhere:
    `a boiler, economiser or other pressure vessel or apparatus, or its contents` -- Peril 2
    `an awning, blind, sign or other external fixture`                     -- Peril 5 excl. (d)
    `movable property`                                                     -- Peril 5 excl. (d), with "in the open"
    `a bank draft or stamp`                                                -- Part 3 helper
    `an electronic data processing medium`                                 -- General Exclusion 7(b)

§§ `A loss under Part 1`

-- The proximate cause, one of the nine Insured Perils (Rủi Ro Được Bảo Hiểm) or another cause.
-- Peril 4 has five limbs, (a)-(e); Peril 5 names six events; Peril 8 two kinds of impact.
-- src:163 | Rủi Ro Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:164 | Là các rủi ro được liệt kê cụ thể sau đây được bảo hiểm trong Phần I – Thiệt Hại Vật Chất theo các
-- src:165 | điều khoản và điều kiện của Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm:
DECLARE `A cause of loss` IS ONE OF
    `fire`                                                    -- Peril 1
    `explosion`                                               -- Peril 2
    `lightning`                                               -- Peril 3
    `riot or civil disturbance`                               -- Peril 4(a)
    `lawful authority suppressing a disturbance`              -- Peril 4(b)
    `wilful act of a striker or locked-out worker`            -- Peril 4(c)
    `lawful authority suppressing a striker's act`            -- Peril 4(d)
    `malicious act of any person`                             -- Peril 4(e)
    `earthquake`                                              -- Peril 5
    `volcanic eruption`                                       -- Peril 5
    `storm`                                                   -- Peril 5, giông lốc
    `whirlwind`                                               -- Peril 5, gió xoáy
    `typhoon`                                                 -- Peril 5, bão
    `flood`                                                   -- Peril 5, lụt
    `escape of water from a tank, apparatus or pipe`          -- Peril 6
    `sprinkler leakage`                                       -- Peril 7
    `impact by aircraft or articles dropped from it`          -- Peril 8(a)
    `impact by a vehicle or animal`                           -- Peril 8(b)
    `theft or attempted theft`                                -- Peril 9
    `seaquake, tidal wave or hail`                            -- named by Extension 7 only
    `another cause`

-- Whether the property was lost or destroyed (basis of settlement (a)) or damaged ((b)).
-- src:302 | (a) Khi tài sản bị tổn thất hay phá hủy: nếu là Ngôi Nhà thì là chi phí xây dựng lại hoặc trong trường
-- src:311 | (b) Khi tài sản bị thiệt hại: việc sửa chữa thiệt hại và phục hồi phần bị thiệt hại của tài sản trở về tình
DECLARE `An extent of loss` IS ONE OF
    `lost or destroyed`
    `damaged`
    `no physical loss, destruction or damage`

-- Every circumstance a Part 1 or Part 3 property loss can turn on: the exclusions inside the
-- nine Insured Perils, the Part 1 exclusions and the General Exclusions. A tick-box list (see
-- the header). The clause is beside each; the source words are quoted where the rule is.
DECLARE `A circumstance of a loss` IS ONE OF
    -- Peril 1, fire, exclusions (a)-(e)
    `fermentation, natural heating or spontaneous combustion`
    `the property underwent a process involving heat`
    `burning by order of a public authority`
    `forest, bush, grass or jungle fire, or clearing land by fire`
    `scorching, melting or charring without flame`
    -- Peril 3, lightning
    `fluctuation of the electricity supply`
    `evidence shows the damage was caused by lightning`
    -- Peril 4 exclusions (i)-(iii), and the proviso in limb (e)
    `an act of terrorism`
    `civil commotion amounting to a popular rising`
    `wilful erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of computer information`
    `the loss claimed is consequential or indirect`
    `cessation of work or interruption of a process or operation`
    `dispossession by confiscation, commandeering or requisition`
    `dispossession of the Home by unlawful occupation`
    `caused intentionally by the Insured, the Family or the Family's guests`
    `caused intentionally by tenants, guests or their families`
    `the act was intended to further a riot or strike or resist a lockout`
    -- Peril 5 exclusions (a)-(i)
    `frost`
    `hail`
    `subsidence, landslip or landslide`
    `the subsidence or landslip was caused by earthquake or volcanic eruption`
    `the premises were under construction, alteration or repair`
    `all external doors, windows and openings were complete and storm-proof`
    `water or rain`
    `rain or water entered through an opening made by the direct force of a storm`
    `escape of water from a tank, apparatus or pipe as a contributing cause`
    `atmospheric or climatic conditions`
    -- Peril 6 exclusions (a)-(c); Peril 7 conditions (a)-(e)
    `discharge or leakage from an automatic sprinkler system`
    `the Home was vacant or unoccupied when the loss occurred`
    `the loss occurred gradually over time`
    `the leakage was sudden`
    `repairs or alterations to the Home or insured location`
    `the sprinkler system was under repair, removal or extension`
    `freezing`
    `the Insured's neglect`
    `an order of government or any municipal, local or other authority`
    `construction defects or conditions known to the Insured beforehand`
    -- Peril 9, theft
    `force or violence used to enter`
    `force or violence used to leave`
    `entry through an open or unlocked door or window`
    `entry with the consent of the owner or occupier`
    `by deception`
    `by a person lawfully on the premises`
    `with the connivance of the Insured, the Family, an employee or domestic helper`
    `from a part of the Home that is lent, let or sublet`
    `the Insurer consented in writing to the Home being left unattended`
    `the property was already damaged or incomplete before the loss`
    `in a part of the Home other tenants can enter without force`
    -- Part 1 exclusions 1-8
    `scratching, denting, chipping or marring only`
    `wear and tear or depreciation`
    `cleaning, dyeing, alteration, repair or restoration`
    `the action of light or atmospheric conditions`
    `rot, mildew, rust, moths, insects or vermin`
    `any other gradually operating cause`
    `electrical or electronic breakdown or failure to operate`
    `a manufacturer's defect or design defect`
    `unexplained loss or mysterious disappearance`
    `errors of programming, punching, labelling or insertion, or loss of data`
    `pollution or contamination`
    `the pollution or contamination was caused by an insured peril`
    `an insured peril was caused by pollution or contamination`
    `the property is more specifically insured by or for the Insured`
    -- General Exclusions 1-9
    `war, invasion, foreign enemy, hostilities or civil war`
    `mutiny, popular rising, insurrection, rebellion, usurped power, martial law or siege`
    `action taken to control, prevent or suppress war, terrorism or rebellion`
    `confiscation, requisition or destruction by order of government or local authority`
    `nuclear weapons material`
    `ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`
    `radioactive, toxic, explosive or hazardous properties of a nuclear explosive assembly`
    `asbestos`
    `DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, AIDS, ARC or a similar syndrome`
    `a wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured or a person acting for the Insured`
    `loss, distortion, erasure or alteration of Electronic Data`
    `a Defined Peril (fire or explosion) resulting from it caused physical loss`
    `cover or payment would breach a sanction of the UN, EU, UK or USA`

-- One loss under Part 1, as the adjuster finds it. `consecutive days the Home had been left
-- unattended` is the count Peril 9 exclusion (d) turns on; GC3(d) has its own count of days
-- vacant, in `The Insured's conduct`.
DECLARE `A Part 1 loss` HAS
    `the item claimed`                                 IS A `A Part 1 item`
    `the property`                                     IS A LIST OF `A description of property`
    `whose property`                                   IS AN `An owner of property`
    `where the property was`                           IS A `A place where property was`
    `the date of the loss`                             IS A DATE
    `the cause`                                        IS A `A cause of loss`
    `the circumstances`                                IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
    `the extent`                                       IS AN `An extent of loss`
    `sudden and unforeseen`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive days the Home had been left unattended` IS A NUMBER

-- A pair or set, for the "Pairs and Sets" clause:
-- src:324 | Cặp và Bộ
-- src:325 | Với bất kỳ hạng mục được bảo hiểm nào bao gồm các vật đi thành đôi hoặc bộ, trách nhiệm của Công
-- src:326 | Ty Bảo Hiểm không vượt quá giá trị của bất kỳ phần hoặc các phần cụ thể nào có thể bị tổn thất hoặc
-- src:327 | thiệt hại mà không tính đến giá trị đặc biệt có thể có của vật hoặc các vật đó như là một phần thuộc cặp
-- src:328 | hoặc bộ vật đó, và cũng không vượt quá tỷ lệ của khoản tiền được bảo hiểm cho cặp hoặc bộ đó.
-- `the sum insured on the pair or set` is NOTHING unless the Summary insures it as such.
DECLARE `A pair or set` HAS
    `the value of the parts lost, without special value as a pair or set` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of parts lost or damaged`                                IS A NUMBER
    `the number of parts in the pair or set`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the sum insured on the pair or set`                                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The figures a Part 1 settlement turns on, as the adjuster states them. Each is a fact
-- about the loss; how they combine is the settlement rule in homecare-part1.l4.
-- `the cost of reinstatement`: basis of settlement (a) or (b), to a condition equal to but
--   not better than new.
-- `the Actual Value`: the defined Giá Trị Thực Tế, new cost less wear and tear (src:286-289).
-- `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost`: Provision 2's comparator;
--   NOTHING is allowed only where the property was lost or destroyed.
-- `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible`: GC6, last paragraph; NOTHING where no
--   regulation prevents reinstatement.
-- `the amount already paid on this item in the Period`, `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the
--   sum insured`: General Limit (b).
-- `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss`: GC9 contribution.
DECLARE `The figures for a Part 1 loss` HAS
    `the cost of reinstatement`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the Actual Value`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the pair or set`                                                IS A MAYBE `A pair or set`
    `the amount already paid on this item in the Period`             IS A NUMBER
    `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss`          IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- The costs claimed under Part 1 Extensions 2-6, as incurred.
DECLARE `The costs claimed under the Part 1 Extensions` HAS
    `the claim for this loss`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `architects', surveyors' and engineers' fees incurred`           IS A NUMBER
    `the fees allowed by the scales of the professional bodies`      IS A NUMBER
    `fire fighting costs incurred`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `costs of removing debris`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `costs of dismantling or demolishing`                            IS A NUMBER
    `costs of shoring or propping up`                                IS A NUMBER
    `costs of temporary protection`                                  IS A NUMBER

§§ `A claim under Part 2`

-- Who is held liable. Part 2 has its own definition of the Insured, limbs (a)-(c):
-- src:490 | Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:491 | Mỗi liệt kê dưới đây được xem như là một Người Được Bảo Hiểm theo Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm trong
-- src:492 | phạm vi bảo hiểm đã được quy định tại Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm:
-- src:493 | (a) Người Được Bảo Hiểm được nêu trong Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm;
-- src:494 | (b) người thân trong Gia Đình Người Được Bảo Hiểm, dù có sống chung với Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:495 | hay không;
-- src:496 | (c) nhân viên trong gia đình của Người Được Bảo Hiểm khi đang làm việc tại Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm
-- src:497 | trong giờ làm việc;
DECLARE `A person held liable` IS ONE OF
    `the Insured named in the Policy Summary`
    `a relative of the Insured`                    -- limb (b)
    `a domestic employee of the Insured`           -- limb (c)
        HAS `working at the Insured Location in working hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another person`

-- The harm the liability is for: Bodily Injury (Thương Tật Thân Thể) and Property Damage
-- (Thiệt Hại về Tài sản), each as Part 2 defines it.
-- src:482 | Thương Tật Thân Thể
-- src:483 | Thương tật thân thể (kể cả tử vong và bệnh tật), tàn tật, hoảng sợ, sốc, đau đớn hoặc tổn thương thần
-- src:484 | kinh.
-- src:485 | Thiệt Hại về Tài sản
-- src:486 | (a) Thiệt hại về vật chất hoặc sự phá hoại tài sản hữu hình, bao gồm việc mất sử dụng phát sinh từ
-- src:487 | sự thiệt hại vật chất hoặc phá hủy nêu trên; hoặc
-- src:488 | (b) Việc mất sử dụng tài sản hữu hình, chưa bị thiệt hại hoặc phá hủy về vật chất, với điều kiện là tổn
-- src:489 | thất này do một Sự Cố gây ra.
DECLARE `A kind of harm` IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `bodily injury, illness or disability`
    `fright, shock, mental anguish or nervous injury`
    `physical damage to or destruction of tangible property`
    `loss of use of tangible property that is not physically damaged`

-- The person injured, for Part 2 exclusions 3 and 4. The day counts are the ones the
-- "usually resides with" definition in exclusion 3 turns on:
-- src:541 | Trong điều khoản loại trừ này, một người được xem là thường sống chung với Người Được Bảo
-- src:542 | Hiểm nếu người đó:
-- src:543 |  đã sử dụng Ngôi Nhà, hoặc
-- src:544 |  đang sống chung với Người Được Bảo Hiểm và dự định hoặc đã dự định sử dụng Ngôi Nhà
-- src:545 | làm nơi ở chính của mình trong 60 ngày hoặc sử dụng hoặc sống với Người Được Bảo Hiểm
-- src:546 | hơn 90 ngày liên tục (bất kể ngày hiệu lực của Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm là ngày nào), mà trong
-- src:547 | thời gian đó có xảy ra Sự Cố.
DECLARE `A person injured` HAS
    `relation to the Insured`                                           IS A MAYBE `A relation`
    `regularly lives with the Insured at the Insured Location`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `has used the Home`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `has used the Home as a place to live`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the Insured`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the person intends or intended to make the Home the main residence` IS A NUMBER
    `consecutive days the person used the Home or lived with the Insured` IS A NUMBER
    `employed by the Insured or a resident and injured in that work`    IS A BOOLEAN

-- The property damaged, for Part 2 exclusion 6 and the tenant's liability extension.
DECLARE `A third party's property` HAS
    `owned or controlled by the Insured, the Family or a resident`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `belonging to an employee of the Insured`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured Location or its fixtures, rented by the Insured`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- Where the liability was established, for the Jurisdiction clause (QUYỀN PHÁN QUYẾT):
-- src:465 | Số tiền bồi thường được quy định trong Phần này sẽ không áp dụng đối với những yêu cầu bồi thường
-- src:466 | được đưa ra hoặc những hành động được thực hiện hoặc những phán quyết không phải là phán quyết
-- src:467 | sơ thẩm của tòa án có thẩm quyền tại Việt Nam hoặc các lệnh do tòa án Việt Nam đưa ra để thi hành
-- src:468 | các phán quyết của tòa án nước ngoài, cho dù dưới hình thức là thỏa thuận có đi có lại hoặc một hình
-- src:469 | thức khác.
DECLARE `A forum` IS ONE OF
    `a first-instance judgment of a competent Vietnamese court`
    `an appellate judgment of a Vietnamese court`
    `a claim settled without judgment`
    `a judgment of a foreign court`
    `a Vietnamese order enforcing a foreign judgment`

-- Every circumstance a Part 2 claim can turn on: the 17 Part 2 exclusions and the tenant's
-- liability extension. A tick-box list (see the header).
DECLARE `A circumstance of a liability` IS ONE OF
    `an intentional act of the Insured or a Family member`              -- excl. 1
    `a negligent act of the Insured or a Family member`                 -- excl. 1, "chểnh mảng"
    `the consequences were reasonably foreseeable from the act`         -- excl. 1
    `liability assumed by agreement that would not otherwise attach`    -- excl. 2
    `the agreement is the tenancy agreement`                            -- tenant's extension
    `the tenancy agreement was sent to the Insurer`                     -- tenant's extension
    `a workers' compensation law, judgment, agreement or scheme`        -- excl. 5
    `business, trade or profession of the Insured, Family or a resident` -- excl. 7
    `construction, alteration, repair or decoration of the Home`        -- excl. 8
    `aircraft or aerial device (other than a model or toy kite) or airfield` -- excl. 9(a)
    `motor boat or vessel, jetty or mooring`                            -- excl. 9(b)
    `a road-licensed or compulsorily insured vehicle, or its loading`   -- excl. 9(c)
    `email, advertising or internet communication`                      -- excl. 9(d)
    `transmission of a communicable disease`                            -- excl. 10
    `use of an Insured Location or land other than as a private residence` -- excl. 11
    `the cost of performing, completing, correcting or improving work`  -- excl. 12
    `goods made, sold or supplied by the Insured and no longer in its control` -- excl. 13
    `food or drink poisoning at the Insured Location`                   -- excl. 13, carve-back
    `the Insured took every possible precaution with food and drink`    -- excl. 13, proviso
    `giving or failing to give professional advice or service`          -- excl. 14
    `pollution or contamination`                                        -- excl. 15
    `fines, penalties or liquidated damages`                            -- excl. 16
    `punitive, exemplary or multiplied damages`                         -- excl. 17

DECLARE `A Part 2 claim` HAS
    `the person held liable`                           IS A `A person held liable`
    `the date of the Occurrence`                       IS A DATE
    `at or near the Insured Location`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `connected with the ownership or use of the Home`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `unexpected and unintended by the Insured`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `legally liable`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm`                                         IS A LIST OF `A kind of harm`
    `the person injured`                               IS A MAYBE `A person injured`
    `the property damaged`                             IS A MAYBE `A third party's property`
    `the circumstances`                                IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a liability`
    `the general circumstances`                        IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
    `the forum`                                        IS A `A forum`

-- The figures a Part 2 payment turns on.
DECLARE `The figures for a Part 2 claim` HAS
    `the damages for which the Insured is liable`      IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant's costs recovered from the Insured`  IS A NUMBER
    `costs incurred with the Insurer's written consent` IS A NUMBER
    `paid under Part 2 earlier in the Period`          IS A NUMBER
    `paid for food and drink earlier in the Period`    IS A NUMBER

§§ `Claims under Part 3`

-- The capacity in which the Insured claims the temporary accommodation benefit, limb 1
-- (rent, as landlord not occupying) or limb 2 (as occupier or owner-occupier):
-- src:632 | 1. Tiền cho thuê phải thanh toán cho Người Được Bảo Hiểm với tư cách là chủ nhà nhưng không sử
-- src:633 | dụng Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm.
-- src:639 | 2. Chi phí hợp lý Phát sinh thêm cho Chỗ ở Tạm thời với tư cách là Người sử dụng hoặc Người sử dụng
-- src:640 | kiêm Chủ sở hữu Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm đó.
DECLARE `A capacity` IS ONE OF
    `landlord not occupying the Insured Location`
    `occupier`
    `owner-occupier`

DECLARE `A temporary accommodation claim` HAS
    `the damage to the Home`                           IS A `A Part 1 loss`
    `the Home is unfit for occupation`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the capacity`                                     IS A `A capacity`
    `months needed to restore or repair the Home`      IS A NUMBER
    `rent lost`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `additional cost of temporary accommodation`       IS A NUMBER
    `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period`    IS A NUMBER

-- What caused the death benefit injury: the clause names fire and theft.
-- src:657 | Nếu Người Được Bảo Hiểm, được nêu tên trong Bản Tóm Tắt Hợp Đồng Bảo Hiểm theo Phần này, bị
-- src:658 | thương tật trầm trọng khi đang ở trong Địa Điểm Bảo Hiểm do hậu quả của cháy hoặc trộm cắp gây ra
-- src:659 | và trường hợp thương tật thân thể như đã nêu dẫn đến tử vong cho Người Được Bảo Hiểm trong vòng
-- src:660 | 3 tháng, Công Ty Bảo Hiểm sẽ thanh toán bồi thường cho người đại diện của Người Được Bảo Hiểm.
DECLARE `A cause of injury` IS ONE OF
    `fire`
    `theft`
    `another cause`

DECLARE `A death benefit claim` HAS
    `the date of the injury`                           IS A DATE
    `the date of death`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `seriously injured`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Insured Location when injured`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause of the injury`                          IS A `A cause of injury`
    `the circumstances`                                IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
    `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period`    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `A domestic helper claim` HAS
    `requested by the Insured`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss`                                         IS A `A Part 1 loss`
    `the helper observed the terms as if the Insured`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the helper is entitled under another insurance`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the loss`                           IS A NUMBER
    `paid under this benefit earlier in the Period`    IS A NUMBER

§§ `The Insured's conduct, for the General Conditions`

-- The facts the General Conditions turn on, for one claim. Each is a matter of record or of
-- testimony: what the Insured did, when, and what the Insurer did in reply.
-- GC1 (due observance), GC2 (misdescription), GC3(a)-(e) (alterations), GC4(a)-(g) (claims
-- procedure), GC5 (obstruction), GC7 (forfeiture), GC12 (precautions), and Part 1's proof of
-- value. A MAYBE DATE is NOTHING where the thing has not happened.
DECLARE `The Insured's conduct` HAS
    `observed and fulfilled the terms of the policy`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statements in the Proposal Form were true`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `misrepresented, misdescribed or omitted a matter in a document`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insurer elected to avoid the policy for misdescription`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insured Location was used other than as a residence`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property was moved to another building or place`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive days the Home had been vacant`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Insurer endorsed its consent before the loss`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave immediate written notice with full particulars`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `forwarded every writ, summons and notice on receipt`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `admitted or offered payment without written consent`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified the police immediately`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `acted immediately to minimise the loss`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed all other insurances`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the written claim was delivered`                          IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date to which the Insurer extended time in writing`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `kept receipts or proof of value`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable precautions`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `obstructed or failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is fraudulent in any respect`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `used fraudulent means or devices`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the claim was rejected`                                   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the rejection was challenged`                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of an arbitral award on the claim`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the award was challenged`                                 IS A MAYBE DATE

-- A cancellation under GC11, by either party.
DECLARE `A cancellation` HAS
    `cancelled by`                                     IS A `A party`
    `the date the cancellation takes effect`           IS A DATE
